{title: Scarborough Fair}
{artist: Traditional}
{key: Dm}
{tempo: 92}
{time: 3/4}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Dm]Are you going to [C]Scarborough [Dm]Fair?
[F]Parsley, [Dm]sage, rose[C]mary and [Dm]thyme
[Dm]Remember [F]me to one who [C]lives there
[Dm]She once [C]was a true love of [Dm]mine
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Dm]Tell her to make me a [C]cambric [Dm]shirt
[F]Parsley, [Dm]sage, rose[C]mary and [Dm]thyme
[Dm]Without no [F]seams nor [C]needlework
[Dm]Then she'll [C]be a true love of [Dm]mine
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Dm]Tell her to find me an [C]acre of [Dm]land
[F]Parsley, [Dm]sage, rose[C]mary and [Dm]thyme
[Dm]Between the salt [F]water and the [C]sea strand
[Dm]Then she'll [C]be a true love of [Dm]mine
{end_of_verse}
